    "narrative": "With the team facing a light schedule today, the focus shifts to maximizing efficiency in the 5x5 categories, particularly our need to bolster stolen bases given their scarcity in the current landscape. **Jorge Polanco** holds the lone active start for the Austin Waves today, carrying a marginal 51.30 score against Nola, A. While his matchup is tempered by the opposing pitcher\u2019s 3.87 xERA and a 5% penalty for the right-on-right platoon disadvantage, he remains our primary engine for runs and RBI. A 31% rain risk in Philadelphia looms over his availability, making him a volatile play, but he is our best option to chase production while high-impact bats like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** are sidelined due to an organization-wide team off-day.\n\nThe bench remains stagnant, as the core roster of **Luis Robert Jr.** (IL), **Andy Pages**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Cole Carrigg**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Curtis Mead**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Lara**, and **Denzer Guzman** are all effectively out of commission today. The decision to bench our high-ceiling talent was forced by the schedule, but it reinforces the need to preserve our daily game caps for more favorable splits later in the week. We will closely monitor the weather reports in Philadelphia for **Jorge Polanco**; if the rain forces a delay or postponement, we have no viable bench alternatives to pivot to, effectively yielding our offensive categories for the July 16 slate.",
